{"term":"Tunte","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"effeminate_gay_man","concept":"gay_queen","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":65,"technical":2,"recognition_pct_current":92,"recognition_pct_peak":92,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"An effeminate or flamboyant gay man; used as a slur but increasingly reclaimed within German LGBTQ+ communities.","english_term":"fairy","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Root word for compound slurs Tuntenschwein and Tuntenalarm; community reclamation is well underway in German queer spaces."}
{"term":"Warmer Bruder","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"gay_man","concept":"gay_man_slur","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"dated_slang","crude":45,"technical":2,"recognition_pct_current":75,"recognition_pct_peak":85,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'warm brother'; a dated German slur for a gay man, alluding to male body warmth in shared beds or bodily contact.","english_term":"fairy","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Etymological origin disputed; 'warm' in this compound alludes to the warmth of male-male bodily proximity; attested from the 19th century."}
{"term":"Warmer","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"gay_man","concept":"gay_man_slur","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"dated_slang","crude":40,"technical":2,"recognition_pct_current":62,"recognition_pct_peak":78,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Ellipsis of 'warmer Bruder'; a dated German slur for a gay man.","english_term":"fairy","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The shortened form; functions identically to the full phrase but is somewhat more opaque to younger speakers unfamiliar with the idiom's origin."}
{"term":"Homo","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"homosexual","concept":"homosexual_slur","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":40,"technical":10,"recognition_pct_current":97,"recognition_pct_peak":97,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Derogatory abbreviation of 'Homosexueller'; used as a slur for a gay man, though somewhat milder in German discourse than some English equivalents.","english_term":"homo","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Direct cross-linguistic cognate with identical function and roughly equivalent severity; remains common as a schoolyard insult."}
{"term":"Päderast","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"gay_man","concept":"homosexual_slur","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"archaic","crude":55,"technical":30,"recognition_pct_current":52,"recognition_pct_peak":70,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'pederast'; historically used in German as a broad slur for any gay man, derived from the Greek institutionalized practice of adult-male-adolescent relationships.","english_term":"pederast","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"In modern German carries both the specific classical sense and the broader historical use as a catch-all legal and moral condemnation of gay men; legal registers once used it synonymously with §175 violations."}
{"term":"§175er","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"gay_man","concept":"homosexual_slur","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"dated_slang","crude":50,"technical":18,"recognition_pct_current":50,"recognition_pct_peak":68,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"A man prosecuted or identified under Paragraph 175 of the German Criminal Code, which criminalized male homosexual acts from 1871 to 1994; used as a slur for gay men.","english_term":"sodomite","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"§175 was partially decriminalized in West Germany in 1969 and fully repealed in reunified Germany in 1994; the term carries especially heavy historical stigma tied to Nazi persecution, during which roughly 100,000 men were charged."}
{"term":"Hundertfünfundsiebziger","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"gay_man","concept":"homosexual_slur","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"dated_slang","crude":45,"technical":12,"recognition_pct_current":35,"recognition_pct_peak":58,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"The number 175 spelled out in full; a circumlocution for §175er, used to identify or slur gay men by indirect reference to the criminal code.","english_term":"sodomite","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The spelled-out form provided a layer of plausible deniability or coded register; less recognized today than the numeral shorthand, especially among younger speakers."}
{"term":"Arschficker","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"gay_man","concept":"gay_man_slur","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":92,"technical":15,"recognition_pct_current":85,"recognition_pct_peak":85,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'ass fucker'; a highly offensive German slur for a gay man; also used as a general-purpose insult for any contemptible person regardless of sexuality.","english_term":"ass fucker","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Dual function as anti-gay slur and general insult; literal anatomical reference makes it among the crudest entries in this section; the general-insult use has largely displaced the specifically anti-gay use in younger registers."}
{"term":"Hintenrum","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"gay","concept":"gay","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"euphemism","crude":25,"technical":2,"recognition_pct_current":80,"recognition_pct_peak":80,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'around the back' or 'back way'; a German euphemism for homosexuality, using anal sex as a synecdoche for gay male identity.","english_term":"the back way","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"'Er ist hintenrum' = 'he is gay'; more euphemistic than most entries in this section; tone determines whether pejorative or merely indirect."}
{"term":"Süßer","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"effeminate_gay_man","concept":"effeminate_man_slur","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":20,"technical":2,"recognition_pct_current":52,"recognition_pct_peak":58,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'sweet one' or 'sweetie'; used as a mildly coded or mocking term for an effeminate gay man, though the same word functions as a generic term of endearment.","english_term":"sweetie","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The gay-identity reading requires tonal and contextual cues; without them the word is entirely unremarkable; recognition as a gay slur specifically is low outside older cohorts."}
{"term":"Butterblume","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"effeminate_gay_man","concept":"effeminate_man_slur","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"dated_slang","crude":35,"technical":2,"recognition_pct_current":28,"recognition_pct_peak":50,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'buttercup'; dated German slang for an effeminate, weak, or gay man, using flower imagery to imply delicacy and sexual deviance.","english_term":"pansy","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Parallels English 'pansy' in mechanism and era; flower-coded slurs for effeminate men are cross-linguistically common; largely out of active use in contemporary German."}
{"term":"verkehrt","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"gay","concept":"queer_identity","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"dated_slang","crude":28,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":52,"recognition_pct_peak":68,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'wrong' or 'inverted'; a dated German descriptor for homosexuality implying moral or natural incorrectness, echoing 19th-century sexological inversion theory.","english_term":"inverted","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Mirrors the 19th-century clinical concept of 'sexual inversion'; functions historically like English 'queer' in its pejorative sense of wrongness or reversal from the norm."}
{"term":"andersrum","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"gay","concept":"gay","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":15,"technical":2,"recognition_pct_current":88,"recognition_pct_peak":88,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'the other way around'; a common, relatively neutral German colloquialism for being gay or homosexual.","english_term":"the other way","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Among the least pejorative entries in this section; 'Er ist andersrum' is everyday colloquial usage and often carries no strong negative charge; widely used across age groups."}
{"term":"Transe","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"transgender","concept":"transgender_slur","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":70,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":88,"recognition_pct_peak":88,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"A derogatory German term for a transgender or cross-dressing person; the approximate German equivalent of English 'tranny'.","english_term":"tranny","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Widely considered offensive by German transgender communities; derived from 'Transvestit' or 'Transsexuell'; still appears in tabloid media, sometimes without awareness of its offensive status."}
{"term":"Zwitterwesen","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"intersex","concept":"intersex","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":42,"technical":35,"recognition_pct_current":48,"recognition_pct_peak":48,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'hermaphrodite being' or 'hybrid creature'; applied to intersex, non-binary, or transgender people with a dehumanizing implication carried by the 'Wesen' (creature) suffix.","english_term":"hermaphrodite","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"'Zwitter' alone is the standard German word for hermaphrodite; adding 'Wesen' (being/creature) amplifies the othering, quasi-zoological quality; usage is declining as clinical and advocacy language spreads."}
{"term":"Lesbe","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"lesbian","concept":"lesbian_slur","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":45,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":97,"recognition_pct_peak":97,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"The standard German word for 'lesbian,' weaponized pejoratively as an insult targeting women perceived as lesbian or insufficiently feminine.","english_term":"lesbian","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"In neutral use 'Lesbe' is the ordinary German word for lesbian and carries no inherent offense; the pejorative function emerges entirely from tone, context, and intent; the word itself is neutral, the slur is in the deployment."}
{"term":"Tribade","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"lesbian","concept":"lesbian","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"archaic","crude":20,"technical":48,"recognition_pct_current":20,"recognition_pct_peak":38,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"A historical term borrowed from Greek for a woman who has sex with other women; the classical and early modern German term for a lesbian.","english_term":"tribade","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"'Tribade' exists in English too as a classical/archaic term; from Greek 'tribein' (to rub); found in 18th–19th century German medical, legal, and literary texts; essentially extinct in living usage."}
{"term":"Mannweib","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"butch_lesbian","concept":"butch_lesbian_slur","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":60,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":70,"recognition_pct_peak":78,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'man-woman'; a derogatory German compound for a masculine-presenting woman, typically targeting butch lesbians.","english_term":"mannish woman","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Parallels English 'bull dyke' or 'mannish lesbian' as a compound insult conflating gender nonconformity with lesbian identity; 'Weib' carries additional contempt as a degrading form of 'woman'."}
{"term":"Schwesterlein","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"effeminate_gay_man","concept":"gay_queen","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"dated_slang","crude":22,"technical":2,"recognition_pct_current":38,"recognition_pct_peak":55,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'little sister'; a dated coded term used within or mockingly toward gay men, implying effeminacy or gay community membership.","english_term":"sister","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"'Sister' occupies a similar in-group/out-group role in English gay community speech; the diminutive '-lein' suffix adds either a condescending or camp-affectionate quality depending on speaker."}
{"term":"Lila Lavendel","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"gay","concept":"gay","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"dated_slang","crude":15,"technical":2,"recognition_pct_current":30,"recognition_pct_peak":46,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'purple lavender'; a dated coded German phrase for homosexuality, referencing the historical association of lavender and violet colors with gay identity.","english_term":"lavender","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Lavender and violet have signified gay identity across Western cultures since at least the early 20th century; the phrase functions as both coded euphemism and camp/ironic slur; now largely supplanted by more direct language."}
{"term":"Tante","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"effeminate_gay_man","concept":"gay_queen","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":25,"technical":2,"recognition_pct_current":65,"recognition_pct_peak":70,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'aunt'; used as a coded term or mild slur for an older or effeminate gay man, analogous to 'auntie' in English gay slang.","english_term":"auntie","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Within German gay communities 'Tante' can be affectionate or camp; used by outsiders it is mildly mocking; 'alte Tante' (old aunt) is a more dismissive variant targeting older gay men."}
{"term":"Tuntenschwein","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"effeminate_gay_man","concept":"gay_man_slur","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":88,"technical":2,"recognition_pct_current":45,"recognition_pct_peak":50,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'fairy-pig'; a compound intensifier combining Tunte (effeminate gay man) with Schwein (pig) to produce a maximally contemptuous slur for a flamboyant gay man.","english_term":"fucking fairy","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"'Schwein' (pig) functions as a general contempt amplifier in German compound insults; considerably more hostile and less reclaimed than 'Tunte' alone; niche usage."}
{"term":"Tuntenalarm","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"identities_orientations","subcategory":"effeminate_gay_man","concept":"gay_queen","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":38,"technical":2,"recognition_pct_current":40,"recognition_pct_peak":46,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'fairy alarm'; a humorous or derogatory compound signaling the conspicuous arrival or presence of one or more flamboyant gay men.","english_term":"queen alert","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Functions as in-group camp humor among gay men or as a derogatory outside observation depending on speaker; the 'alarm' framing implies unwanted or excessive visibility; no precise English equivalent."}
{"term":"Stricher","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"sex_work_pornography","subcategory":"male_sex_worker","concept":"sex_worker","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":45,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":72,"recognition_pct_peak":80,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"A male street sex worker or hustler; from 'Strich' (the strip or street beat where sex workers solicit clients); frequently implies gay or bisexual male clientele.","english_term":"hustler","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"'Strich' refers to the specific street or area where sex workers operate; usage skews toward male gay street prostitution but is not exclusively so; placement in the identities/slurs section of German sexual lexicons reflects the historical conflation of gay identity with criminalized sex work under §175."}
{"term":"Strichjunge","lang":"de","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"sex_work_pornography","subcategory":"male_sex_worker","concept":"sex_worker","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":55,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":62,"recognition_pct_peak":70,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Literally 'hustler boy'; a young male street sex worker; the '-junge' suffix emphasizes youth within the Stricher category, typically implying a teenage or young adult male.","english_term":"rent boy","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"'Junge' (boy) implies youth; British English 'rent boy' is the closest equivalent; carries connotations of poverty-driven male street prostitution serving gay or bisexual clients."}
